Now "Costs and risks" each with item:
- Keeping R10's second sentence live costs a re-measurement and a keep/withdraw decision for every scaffolding item whenever a model changes — work that ships no feature (my #6, my #8). The price of not doing it is scaffolding that masks a capable model and taxes every run.
- Logging and the insight are now SHOULD, so a run can skip them and not be wrong; that is the price of the house rule's "method is SHOULD at most", and it weakens R12 as drafted (my #16 — the level must match the consequence).
- The six whys cost time at the end of a failing task, after the work is already late (my #8, "value victory and not duration" — spend it once, at the end, not on every step).
- The with/without comparison in part 5 needs two runs; done per item it is a second levy (my #8, "does not levy twice"). Run it per scaffolding item only when the model actually changed.
- Config is advice only: if you do not act on it, a root cause the six whys found stays unfixed, and the loop leaks (my #13 — the road not taken has a price).
- Part 6 can be misread as permission to delete checks; a check withdrawn on a comparison nobody set is exactly the "general's fault" the fails-if names (my #15).
- The review rests on someone noticing the model changed; if no one measures, "as models improve" is a claim that cannot fail (my #2 — do not rely on the other side's move; own the trigger).

